close Video Rescue crews in Nepal save two men trapped in tunnels for nine days following floods On Friday morning, searchers heard men's voices, which prompted an all-out rescue mission with the help of the Nepal Army. (Credit: Nepali Army via Storyful)

NEW You can now listen to Fox News articles!

Rescue teams in Nepal pulled two workers alive from a hydropower tunnel nine days after catastrophic floods swept through the country, leaving more than 1,000 people dead and thousands more missing.

